      <div class='hap-note-content'>
        <h3>HAP's Confession:</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>I wrote separate if statements instead of else if — my robot got classified as BOTH "Warm" AND "Optimal" at the same time!</li>
          <li>I put my conditions in the wrong order — checked <code>> 60</code> before <code>> 90</code> and everything was "Optimal."</li>
          <li>I forgot the final else — when <code>coreTemperature</code> was exactly 60, nothing happened and <code>temperatureStatus</code> was undefined.</li>
          <li>I used <code>=</code> instead of <code>===</code> in my condition — assigned instead of compared and broke everything!</li>
